# Production build configuration for the deployed API.
#
# This file is committed on purpose. It contains no secrets — only the public
# URL of the Render service — and committing it means the Vercel build picks up
# the right API address without anyone having to remember to set a variable.
#
# Why a committed file rather than a Vercel dashboard variable: Vite inlines
# `VITE_*` values into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time. Setting the variable
# after the first deploy has no effect until a redeploy, which is an easy way to
# ship a broken build. A committed file makes the value reviewable in a pull
# request and changeable in one place.
#
# Keep the trailing /api — the backend mounts every route under /api and the
# frontend appends paths like /auth/login to this value.
VITE_API_URL=https://baby-vaccination-system.onrender.com/api
